# CrossGuard Deployment Configuration
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# OPTION 1: Dynamic GitHub Gist Registry (Recommended for Google Colab)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# When Colab restarts, its Cloudflare tunnel URL changes. The Colab worker automatically
# publishes its current URL to this fixed GitHub Gist. CrossGuard discovers the worker
# URL automatically without requiring manual edits to .env on every restart.
#
# Create a public or secret Gist at https://gist.github.com and paste its ID below.
# Example Gist ID: 3a7b9c4d5e6f7a8b9c0d1e2f3a4b5c6d
# CROSSGUARD_GPU_REGISTRY_GIST_ID="<your gist id>"

# Optional: GitHub Personal Access Token (classic with 'gist' scope or fine-grained)
# Required ONLY on the Colab worker to publish/heartbeat updates to the Gist.
# Not required for CrossGuard to read a gist, but a token raises GitHub's read limit from 60 to 5000
# requests/hour. Never commit a real token.
# CROSSGUARD_GPU_REGISTRY_GITHUB_TOKEN="ghp_yourPersonalAccessTokenHere"

# Optional: Registry TTL in seconds before an unrefreshed record is considered stale (default: 300)
# CROSSGUARD_GPU_REGISTRY_TTL=300

# OPTION 2: Static Worker URL Fallback
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Used as a direct worker URL or as a fallback if the registry lookup is unavailable or stale.
# Example: CROSSGUARD_GPU_WORKER_URL="https://example.trycloudflare.com"
# CROSSGUARD_GPU_WORKER_URL="https://<your-worker>.trycloudflare.com"

# Optional: extra hosts a registry-provided worker URL may use (comma separated).
# By default only https://*.trycloudflare.com / *.ngrok-free.app / *.ngrok.io (and localhost) are accepted,
# because the registry is untrusted input and video frames are sent to this URL.
# CROSSGUARD_GPU_ALLOWED_HOSTS="gpu.example.com"
